' 12 Routing decision: how the reducer classifies the channel of a send or a
' receive and maps the class to the default space, a native space, or a user
' agent (rules R1 to R7).
'
' Source of Figure N5 in ../design.md (section N5). The figure restates
' classify_channel and route in rholang/src/rust/interpreter/reified/route.rs,
' the hooks of reified/reducer_hooks.rs, and the R7 backend of
' reified/execution.rs (P4 design C.1 and C.6). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order, from the top to the bottom:
'   1. The reducer removes the bundle of the channel.
'   2. classify_channel gives the channel exactly one class, by the first
'      test that holds.
'   3. route maps the class to a route by the rules R1 to R5.
'   4. A default route makes the baseline call. A space route builds the
'      identity on the data channel (R6) and runs one space job. On an
'      agent route, a send becomes the call A'!(sink, "produce", raw, [d...])
'      on the agent, which routes again with no use context (P8 step 2). A
'      receive whose binds all route to one agent becomes the translation
'      T_recv (P8 step 3): one persistent matcher receive for each bind, the
'      body receive, and last the call A'!(sink, "consume", pairs, arrow, b)
'      on the agent. A mix of targets fails with CrossSpaceJoin, and a query
'      fails with QuerySpecUnsupportedOnAgentSpace.
'   5. A note at the top gives the R7 backend, which routes the replies of
'      system processes with the same rules and no use context. Since P8
'      step 2, the bundle with both flags of an agent-minted name routes to
'      its agent (R7A).
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 12-routing-decision.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 12-routing-decision
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam PartitionBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title Routing decision of a channel (rules R1 to R7)

start
:the reducer evaluates the channel <latex>c</latex> of a send or a receive
and removes its write or read bundle; <<$rrs_host>>
note right
  **R7.** The replies of system processes bypass
  the reducer. The R7 backend routes them with
  these rules and no use context, so a forged
  reply channel goes to the default space.
  **R7A** (P8 step 2): the bundle with both flags
  around an agent-tagged tuple routes to its agent.
end note
partition "classify_channel(c): the first test that holds" {
  if (a sole GPrivate with an id of 1 or 2 bytes?) then (yes)
    :System: a byte name, an op channel, or a marker; <<$rrs_system>>
  elseif (a sole GPrivate whose id decodes to KIND C, H, X, or B?) then (yes)
    :DefaultObject: an object of the default space; <<$rrs_object>>
  elseif (a sole GPrivate whose id decodes to KIND D, I, A, or S?) then (yes)
    :Storage: a storage channel, already routed; <<$rrs_storage>>
  elseif (a sole GPrivate whose id decodes to KIND N?) then (yes)
    :SpaceName(space): a space name; <<$rrs_name>>
  elseif (any other sole unforgeable name?) then (yes)
    :Unforgeable: an ordinary new name; <<$rrs_host>>
  elseif (a tuple (AGENT_TAG, A, raw)?) then (yes)
    :AgentTagged: a name of a user agent; <<$rrs_name>>
  else (no)
    :Forged: any other channel, such as @"jobs"; <<$rrs_host>>
  endif
}
partition "route(space_ctx, c)" {
  switch (class?)
  case (System, DefaultObject, Unforgeable)
    :R1: the default space; <<$rrs_host>>
  case (Storage)
    :R2: the default space; <<$rrs_host>>
  case (SpaceName(space))
    :R3: the collection <latex>\mathrm{canon}(c)</latex> of its own space,
    in every use context; <<$rrs_agent>>
  case (AgentTagged)
    :R4: the user agent A; <<$rrs_name>>
  case (Forged)
    if (a use context?) then (yes)
      :R5: the collection <latex>\mathrm{canon}(c)</latex>
      of the space of the use context; <<$rrs_agent>>
    else (no)
      :R5: the default space; <<$rrs_host>>
    endif
  endswitch
}
switch (route?)
case (default space)
  :the hook makes the baseline call
  with identical arguments; <<$rrs_host>>
case (native space)
  :R6: the identity uses the data channel <latex>D(\mathit{sid}, k)</latex>
  one space job runs the operation; <<$rrs_agent>>
case (user agent)
  if (a send?) then (yes)
    :a send becomes the call <latex>A'</latex>!(sink, "produce", raw, [d…])
    on the agent, which routes again with no use context
    (R1 or R4, P8 step 2); <<$rrs_name>>
  else (a receive)
    if (every bind routes to the agent A, with no query?) then (yes)
      :T_recv (P8 step 3): one persistent matcher receive
      for each bind, the body receive, and last the call
      <latex>A'</latex>!(sink, "consume", pairs, arrow, bundle+{b})
      on the agent, which routes again with no use context; <<$rrs_name>>
    else (no)
      :CrossSpaceJoin for a mix of targets,
      QuerySpecUnsupportedOnAgentSpace for a query; <<$rrs_reject>>
    endif
  endif
endswitch
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_system>     | system class: byte names, op channels, markers |
|<$rrs_object>     | default-space object (KIND C, H, X, B), and the native space whose agent serves it: one space job |
|<$rrs_storage>    | storage channel: KIND D, I, A, S |
|<$rrs_name>       | name class: space names and agent-tagged names |
|<$rrs_host>       | default space and ordinary channels, with the baseline call |
|<$rrs_reject>     | fail closed |
endlegend
@enduml
